  "body": "There is a minor issue with the definition of a **valid IPv4-address string** in the [Host Writing][1] section. \r\n\r\n> A **valid IPv4-address string** must be four sequences of up to three ASCII digits per sequence, each representing a decimal number no greater than 255, and separated from each other by U+002E (.).\r\n\r\nFrom this is is not clear if e.g. `127.0.0.001` is a valid IPv4-address string.\r\nThe parsing section suggests that it is not; the [IPv4 number parser][2] records a validationError for e.g. `001` in Step 4. \r\n\r\n[1]: https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#valid-ipv4-address-string\r\n[2]: https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#ipv4-number-parser",
